max-visits: 1
on-arrival: compa_caida = 1; memorial += 1

= La compañera caída

The news comes the way the worst news comes, in fragments that take weeks to become a fact: one of the compañeras is taken. Not killed — *taken*, which in this war is the word for a door that opens onto something the language does not have a clean way to hold. She was pregnant; the camp knew before the enemy did. What happens to women in the clandestine cells of this state is a thing the survivors will spend the rest of their lives being unable to fully say, and the specific arithmetic of her case — the interrogation aimed at the body that carried the next generation, the child that is born in captivity and does not come back with the mother who does not come back at all — is the war's most private and most unforgivable page.

The column has to be told, and told in a way that neither breaks it nor lies to it. And a decision has to be made about a name, and a fact, and what the movement owes to both.

- @caida_denunciar: Break the silence — get her name, her condition, and what was done to her out to the exile press, the Church, anyone. Make the private crime a public one.
- @caida_rescate: Everything into finding her — the networks, the parque, the risk, on the chance she is alive and reachable.
- @caida_memoria: Neither can reach her now. Enter her fully in the memorial — name, date, the child's name if it can be learned — and make the movement carry her, so the state's forgetting does not win twice.

@caida_denunciar
choose-if: exiliados >= 1 or sup_students >= 20
unavailable-subtitle: Making the private crime public needs a channel to the outside — an exile press, a sympathetic Church, a campus that will carry it. You lack the reach right now.
on-arrival: legitimidad_regimen -= 3; sup_students += 3; sup_middle += 2; feminismo += 4; represion += 2; leyenda += 1

Her name and what was done to her cross the border in a pastoral letter and a mimeographed bulletin and, eventually, a line in a foreign paper the regime cannot suppress abroad. It changes nothing for her and everything for the argument: the state that insists it merely fights subversives is caught, in her case, doing the thing it most needs the world not to know it does. The middle class that shrugged at a dead guerrillero does not shrug at this. The mothers who will one day fill a plaza demanding their disappeared have, in her name, one more reason to come.

- @post_event: Continuar.

@caida_rescate
choose-if: parque >= 4 and inteligencia >= 25
unavailable-subtitle: A rescue from a clandestine cell needs materiel and precise intelligence you do not have — and a blind attempt only adds names.
on-arrival: parque -= 4; inteligencia -= 6; presos += 1; represion += 3; moral_columnas += 2; expediente += 4

You spend the war's scarce blood — the parque, the intelligence, the irreplaceable people — on the chance. Most such attempts fail, and this account will not tell you in advance whether yours is most. But the column needed to know the movement does not write off its own the moment they are behind the wire, and the attempt, win or lose, is the proof: they will risk for you what you are being asked to risk for them. Sometimes it brings someone home. Sometimes it only brings home the certainty of where she was, which the heart, against all sense, still counts as something.

- @post_event: Continuar.

@caida_memoria
on-arrival: memorial += 1; feminismo += 3; moral_columnas -= 2; leyenda += 1

You do the thing that is not a tactic and cannot be one: you make sure she is *kept.* Her full name, the date she was taken, the place, the child's name when the networks finally learn it — entered in the memorial in the careful hand reserved for the pages that matter most, read aloud once to the assembled column so that no one can later pretend she was a rumor. The state's deepest wager is that women like her vanish twice, once into the cell and once into the silence afterward. The movement cannot reach the cell. It can refuse, absolutely, the silence. Some of what a revolution is for cannot be measured in territory. This is that part.

- @post_event: Continuar.
